{"name":"Vineyard Wine","hex":"#684047","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"vineyard","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A grape plantation, especially one used in the production of wine."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/vineyard"},{"term":"wine","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An alcoholic beverage made by fermenting grape juice, with an ABV ranging from 5.5–16%.","An alcoholic beverage made by fermenting other substances, producing a similar ABV."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To entertain (someone) with wine.","To drink wine."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/wine"}],"entries":[{"title":"Vineyard designated wine","blocks":[{"text":"A vineyard designated wine is a wine produced from the product of a single vineyard with that vineyard's name appearing on the wine label."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3a/Alexander_valley_cab.jpg/330px-Alexander_valley_cab.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vineyard_designated_wine","wikidata":"Q7932498"},{"title":"Vineyard","blocks":[{"text":"A vineyard is a plantation of grape-bearing vines. Many vineyards exist for winemaking; others for the production of raisins, table grapes, and non-alcoholic grape juice. The science, practice and study of vineyard production is known as viticulture. Vineyards are often characterised by their terroir, a French term loosely translating as \"a sense of place\" that refers to the specific geographical and geological characteristics of grapevine plantations, which may be imparted to the wine itself."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e5/Vineyards_in_Burgundy_France.jpg/330px-Vineyards_in_Burgundy_France.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vineyard","wikidata":"Q22715"},{"title":"Wine","blocks":[{"text":"Wine is an alcoholic drink made from fermented grape juice. It is produced and consumed in many regions around the world, in a wide variety of styles which are influenced by different varieties of grapes, growing environments, viticulture methods, and production techniques."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/af/Red_and_white_wine_in_glass.jpg/330px-Red_and_white_wine_in_glass.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wine","wikidata":"Q282"},{"title":"Wine red","blocks":[{"text":"The color wine, or wine red, also called bordeaux, vinous, or vinaceous, is a dark shade of red and brown. It is a representation of the typical color of red wine."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/c/c0/Red_Wine_Glass.jpg/330px-Red_Wine_Glass.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wine_red","wikidata":"Q3014419"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/21/Vinepyrennees2.jpg/500px-Vinepyrennees2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/21/Vinepyrennees2.jpg/500px-Vinepyrennees2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The extensive vineyards of the Languedoc-Roussillon region, southern France","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AVinepyrennees2.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6b/Aerial_View_-_Landschaft_Markgr%C3%A4flerland1.jpg/500px-Aerial_View_-_Landschaft_Markgr%C3%A4flerland1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6b/Aerial_View_-_Landschaft_Markgr%C3%A4flerland1.jpg/1280px-Aerial_View_-_Landschaft_Markgr%C3%A4flerland1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thum